___TESTS___

scenarios:
- name: Injects the per-domain tracker for a valid tracking ID
  code: |-
    const mockData = { trackingId: 'aeec6fcf-7138-4742-ac4e-0adc0221c737' };

    mock('injectScript', (url, onSuccess) => {
      assertThat(url).isEqualTo(
        'https://cdn.menoinfra.com/p/aeec6fcf-7138-4742-ac4e-0adc0221c737.js');
      onSuccess();
    });

    runCode(mockData);

    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasCalled();
- name: Honours a branded script host
  code: |-
    const mockData = {
      trackingId: 'aeec6fcf-7138-4742-ac4e-0adc0221c737',
      scriptHost: 'cdn.example.com'
    };

    mock('injectScript', (url, onSuccess) => {
      assertThat(url).isEqualTo(
        'https://cdn.example.com/p/aeec6fcf-7138-4742-ac4e-0adc0221c737.js');
      onSuccess();
    });

    runCode(mockData);

    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasCalled();
- name: Fails cleanly with no tracking ID
  code: |-
    const mockData = {};

    runCode(mockData);

    assertApi('gtmOnFailure').wasCalled();

___NOTES___

Warm AI - Website Visitor Identification

Loads the Warm AI tracker via GTM. Feature-identical to pasting the direct
script into your site's <head>: company-level identification, and person-level
where available.

Setup
  1. Create a tag from this template.
  2. Paste your Tracking ID from the Warm AI dashboard.
  3. Trigger: All Pages (Page View). Fire it as early as you can.
  4. Submit and publish the container.

Install this template by importing template.tpl (Templates > New > Import).
It is not in the Community Template Gallery.

Docs: https://docs.warmai.uk/guides/install

Changelog
  v2.0.0  Load the per-domain tracker (cdn.menoinfra.com/p/<id>.js) instead of
          posting a bespoke event payload. Fixes GTM installs recording nothing
          at all: the v1 endpoint, track.getwarmai.com/api/gtm-track, returns
          404, and the hostname is now served by a worker that only answers
          POST and OPTIONS while v1 sent a GET via sendPixel. Also brings GTM
          installs to parity with direct installs, which v1 never had: it never
          loaded the per-domain script, so it could not carry Radar or the RB2B
          person-level pixel no matter what the endpoint did.

          Permissions drop from six to one. v1 requested send_pixel,
          get_cookies, set_cookies, access_local_storage, get_url, get_referrer
          and logging; v2 requests only inject_script. Session handling, storage
          and consent all live in the tracker now, so the template neither reads
          nor writes anything in the browser.

          Removed parameters: Event Type, Track Scroll Depth, Track Page
          Duration, Custom Tracking Endpoint, Session Timeout. All of these are
          handled by the tracker; they existed only to drive the hand-rolled v1
          payload. Existing tags carry these values harmlessly, but re-create
          the tag if you want a clean config.

  v1.0.0  Initial release. Page view tracking with session management, scroll
          depth and duration. Superseded; do not use.
